WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our first guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.538
who you know from
"The Good Place" and "Frozen."

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.907
She's returning
as the voice of "Gossip Girl"

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.343
beginning July 8th on HBO Max.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.245
Please welcome Kristen Bell!

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.848
Ah! Ah, I'm so happy.

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:17.116
Thank you!

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.385
Oh, so good to see you.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.554
Thank you so much
for coming back on the show.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.855
I appreciate it.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.056
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:26.526
-Oh, please. I don't know
if you just witnessed.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.728
We had some really amazing
talents from around --

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:31.998
-I did.
-You did.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.600
Kind of amazing, right?
Is your mind blown?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.136
-My mind's blown, and I kind of
want to show you mine.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.271
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.974
Yeah. Do you have
a hidden talent?

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:44.010
-Yeah, like a hidden talent
that, like, is totally useless

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.112
and you could never
apply to anything.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.380
-Yes. That's what we want.
-You know?

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.781
Like that kind of talent?
-Yes, we love that!

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.016
-I got one.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:53.218
Jimmy, I have separate control
over my eyeballs.

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:54.554
[ Audience murmuring ]

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.955
-Wait --
-Do you want to see this?

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:56.989
-Yes.
-Okay. Hold on.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.191
I'm going to have to
come in close.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.659
Can you see -- Is that
a good shot? Okay, ready?

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.727
-Yes.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.563
[ Audience groaning ]

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.431
-Wow! Whoa!

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.567 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.303
Wow!

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.272
How -- When did you know
that you could do that?

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.473
-I don't know.

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:17.877
I've always felt like
it was a separate muscle,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.378
and I could always
tap into them.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.747
But I guess I assumed
everybody else had that, too.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.850
And then once in like
high school, I did it,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.218
and my friends
were like, "Whoa!"

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.887
And then I realized
not everybody has it,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.690
and I'll be able to apply it
to absolutely nothing.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.759
-Yeah, absolutely.
That's correct, yeah.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.895
-But I will say,
don't ever sneak up on me,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.897
because I do have
separate control.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.098
-Ah.
-I can look anywhere.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.133
-You see everything. Yeah.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.537
But I want to talk you
about this, 'cause recently,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:48.408
it was just -- came out
that you have a very big fan.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:53.278
President Barack Obama said
on his podcast, much of a fan.

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:54.913
-If you say so, Jimmy.

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:56.582
-No, I'm telling you.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:59.752
It was so --
So, your husband, Dax,

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:04.990
I guess he sent in a question
to Obama's podcast?

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.760
-Mm-hmm. They were asking people
to write in questions,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.296
and he asked a question like,
"What was it --

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.166
Not having a male role model
when you were young,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.134
did that affect
how much you wanted to show off

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.637
to other guys?" Like, you know?

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.606
And, yeah.
And he answered the question

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:25.078
by giving a real big shout-out
to "The Good Place."

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.680
-I want to play everyone
this clip here.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.717
Just check out the shout-out
from President Obama to Kristen.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.602
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.370
-What?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.740
-I mean, is it our destiny
to be best friends?

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.874
-Yes!
-I've always thought that,

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:58.777
but I never knew
he might think it, as well!

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:02.148
-[ Laughs ]
-I mean, when that happened,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:05.852
Dax was like,
"Well, here we go again.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.153
My wife gets credit
for everything."

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.289
Because it was like Dax
was writing in the question

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:12.058
and he --
-"This was my big moment."

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.392
Yeah. "This is my big moment.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:16.862
President Obama's going
to know me, Dax Shepard."

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.430
Instead, he flips it around and
goes,

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.666
"By the way, I love your wife."

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.934
It's so awesome.
-He flipped the script.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.570
Whoops. But I was so flattered.
I mean, we knew --

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.773
We did know, like when
"The Good Place" was happening,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.975
you know, Mike Schur,
who we both know and love,

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:32.378
we definitely found out that
it was, like, on his watch list

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.481
of his favorite TV shows,
and we all freaked out.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:39.018
But, yeah. I never thought I'd
get like a personal shout-out.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.020
And I do think this is destiny

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.756
for a very, very
best friendship.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.591
Not to put any pressure on
anybody, but I know.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.560
-No, no pressure. Yeah.
I'll put you guys in touch.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.994
Yeah, you guys should be pals.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.796
I want to talk about
"Gossip Girl."

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.098
I knew this was coming back.
I'm so excited.

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:54.600
I think it's the right time.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.702
We want it back.

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.472
It's on HBO Max
starting July 8th.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.641
And you're returning
as the voice of "Gossip Girl."

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:03.676
-You know it.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.212
-Yeah, no --
[ Audience cheering ]

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.447
I think you're --
I love your voice, but I mean --

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.148
I love everything.
I love your acting.

00:04:10.148 --> 00:04:11.918
But I think your voice --

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:15.421
Do you like doing voiceovers
and cartoons?

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.390
-I love it.
I mean, I especially --

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.092
You know, I like the challenge

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:23.562
of having to evoke emotion
from the audience

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.365
by using only one tool,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.867
like the tone, pitch,
cadence of my voice.

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.736
It's really fun. And, like, you
know, on "Gossip Girl" --

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.171
Like the new show
is really cool,

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.807
'cause it talks all about
how social media has changed us,

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.243
and it is more risque
'cause it is on HBO Max.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.611
-Yeah.
-And there's a twist

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.013
at the end of episode one
that's really different, but --

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.816
So, that's fun. But that's much
more of, like, a character.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:47.286
And then with "Frozen," it's --
I guess it's also a character

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.055
'cause it is a little
more bubbly than I am.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:52.258
But I just like story-telling,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:55.494
and I like being able
to have the challenge

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:56.628
of only using my voice.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:58.698
Also, like, you know
from V.O.'s you've done,

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.467
you really can go in your
pajamas, and it's great.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.771
But it's also been
the main form of work

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.705
that I've been able to do
during the pandemic,

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.340
because you just
have a microphone,

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.443
and you don't have to have
contact with people.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.411
And it's kind of incredible.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:15.815
And during the pandemic,
Monica Padman,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:19.518
who hosts "Armchair Expert",
my husband's podcast with him,

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:21.353
came up with this idea
for us to do --

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:22.688
We're going to start a podcast

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.924
that will launch in a couple
weeks in the end of June.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:30.095
We interviewed 10,
like, phenomenal women

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:31.697
that have cracked
the glass ceiling

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.632
that we just wanted to talk to.

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:36.536
So we got to interview --
It's called "Shattered Glass."

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.605
And we got to interview,
like, Diane von Furstenberg,

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:42.208
Malala Yousafzai, Oprah,

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.510
I mean, some really
incredible people.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:49.214
But just have like down to Earth
conversations with them

00:05:49.214 --> 00:05:51.817
about their mistakes and
how they care for themselves.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.554
And then we got Sara Bareilles

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:57.823
to sing the theme song with
the Detroit children's choir.

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.558
-I love Sara Bareilles.
-So I got to say, like,

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.060
this behind
the microphone thing,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.763
it might become
the rest of my life.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.864
-Yeah, well, we'll take it.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.033
I'll take any Kristen Bell
I can get.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.535
Here's a first look
at a piece of the trailer

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:12.338
for "Gossip Girl."
Take a look at this.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:15.273 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:15.273 --> 00:06:17.109
-Who waits for the light?

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.378
-She's not from here.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.248
Hey.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:25.918
How would you like
to come hang with us tonight?

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.254
[ Elevator bell dings ]

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:32.057
-♪ Too many joy rides
in Daddy's Jaguar ♪

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:35.995
♪ Too many white lies
and white lines ♪

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:39.665
♪ Super rich kids with nothing
but loose ends ♪

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.200
[ Cellphones chiming,
vibrating ]

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.468
-Did you miss me?

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.236
I know I've missed you.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:46.806
-Oh, my God!
-Yeah!

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.740
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.343
Dude, we're all
going crazy here!

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:53.545
You can check out
the full "Gossip Girl" trailer

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.714
on HBO Max's YouTube page.

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:57.883
Kristen and I are playing a fun
new game when we come back.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:58.918
Stick around, everybody.

